# What the project keeps out of version control.
#
# The rule changed when this became a multi-holding pipeline. It used to publish
# only the finished website; it now has to be able to rebuild that website from
# scratch, so the pipeline and the transcriptions travel with it. What stays out
# is bulk that can be re-derived, or that is not ours.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# COPYRIGHTED SOURCE. The Seidel (2018) biography was kept out from the start
# (2026-09-04): facts and short cited quotations in the edition, never the book.
# The editor ruled otherwise on 2026-10-19, told that the repository is public
# and that committing the book publishes it: the text and Claude's English are
# kept in literature/seidel2018/ for questions, with no page on the site
# (visible: false; docs/LITERATURE_PLAN.md, section 4). The patterns below
# still keep out the editor's copies under their old file names.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Friedrich Ludwig, Fürst zu Hohenlohe-Ingelfingen*
*(2018, Seidel)*

# Archival masters, 1.7 GB. site/assets/scans/ carries the downscaled copies
# the site publishes, regenerated by make_scan_derivatives.py.
pages/

# Model output caches. Real money, and re-derivable by paying again, so they
# stay on this machine and are never published.
/cache/

# Generated review sheets and reports. Rebuilt on demand; the decisions they
# lead to are recorded in units/<slug>/rulings.yml and reference/, both tracked.
/review/

# Build output
site/_site/
site/.jekyll-cache/
site/.jekyll-metadata
site/vendor/
.bundle/

# Working files and one-offs left at the project root (the /* form, not
# /scratch/, so that the exception below can re-include a directory inside it)
/scratch/*
# The Pełzucki 1896 map's working directory committed at the editor's word
# (2026-11-01, "commit everything"): the OCR token files, the red catalogue
# (reds_all.json), the reference numbers, the five-table join and the working
# pages with their build scripts - scratch in name only, the session's raw
# material for the map's number system.
!/scratch/map4456/
# the labelling page's transient working state (the autosave files and the
# server's dated snapshots): real work in progress, but the tracked target
# is maps/pelzucki1896/farms.yml and reds.yml, written by import_farms.py
/scratch/map4456/farm_labels_latest.json
/scratch/map4456/red_labels_latest.json
/scratch/map4456/farm_labels_latest.meta.json
/scratch/map4456/red_labels_latest.meta.json
/scratch/map4456/history/
/scratch/map4456/history-test/
/scratch/map4456/test-state/
/*.txt
/*.csv
/*.json
*.bak*
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# API credential
.anthropic_key

# OS noise
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# The site data generated by the pipeline (site/_data/people.yml and the
# rest), regenerated by pipeline/regenerate.py from the tracked sources. They are
# committed like the corpus's derived files, so the CI gate builds and
# verifies the tree as committed - genealogy.yml included, since the person
# pages render their biography and family sections from it.
